---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PhishingSpotter from '../../components/PhishingSpotter';
---

<Layout title="Interactive Phishing Spotter" description="Practice identifying real-world scam emails in a safe, interactive sandbox.">
  <div class="bg-indigo-50 py-12 border-b border-indigo-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-indigo-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
        Interactive Phishing Spotter
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-indigo-800">
        Scammers rely on you missing the subtle details. Can you spot all the red flags in these simulated emails?
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <PhishingSpotter client:load />

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-12 bg-white border border-slate-200 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Why is this important?</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        Phishing is the #1 way hackers gain access to corporate networks and personal bank accounts. They don't usually "hack" your password; they trick you into giving it to them.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600">
        By training your eye to look for inconsistencies—like slightly misspelled email domains, generic greetings, and dangerous file extensions—you dramatically reduce your risk of becoming a victim.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/learn/phishing-basics" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-600 font-bold hover:text-indigo-800 transition-colors">
          Read the full guide on Phishing
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 ml-1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3"></path></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
